WEBVTT

00:02.167 --> 00:03.836
<i>Previously on</i> Lost:

00:03.919 --> 00:07.089
No matter what happens here
I want you to keep moving.

00:09.425 --> 00:12.636
We caught three of them, the ones
who stayed to blow up the tents.

00:12.719 --> 00:16.004
Once the rock star turns off
whatever's jamming us up,

00:16.098 --> 00:17.380
you need to call my boat.

00:17.474 --> 00:20.436
You're inside a room full of equipment.
There's a blinking yellow light.

00:20.519 --> 00:23.887
You flip the switch.
The light goes off. And you drown.

00:23.981 --> 00:26.692
If you don't, there won't be any rescue.

00:31.029 --> 00:33.866
Des! Hide, Des, there's people in there!

00:33.949 --> 00:37.619
Mikhail, I need you to help me
clean up this mess that I've made.

00:37.703 --> 00:40.247
I need you to kill Charlie.

01:01.185 --> 01:04.313
- What's up?
- What's going on?

01:17.451 --> 01:21.622
<i>You have reached</i>
<i>310-555-0...</i>

02:09.002 --> 02:11.755
- Can I help you?
- Sorry, I...

02:14.716 --> 02:17.209
Actually, I came...

02:19.596 --> 02:21.306
Is the funeral over?

02:21.390 --> 02:25.769
There was no funeral, sir.
Only a viewing. Nobody showed up.

02:27.771 --> 02:31.389
- Nobody? You sure?
- Just you.

02:31.483 --> 02:35.320
My deepest condolences.
Friend or family?

02:39.074 --> 02:40.701
Neither.

02:40.784 --> 02:46.081
- Would you like me to open it up?
- No. No.

02:47.166 --> 02:48.625
Take your time.

03:22.409 --> 03:23.494
Damn it.

03:34.963 --> 03:36.423
Danielle.

03:38.467 --> 03:40.959
- How much further?
- About an hour.

03:42.805 --> 03:45.682
The radio tower.
When was the last time you were there?

03:45.766 --> 03:48.258
The day I recorded the message.

03:49.561 --> 03:53.346
I'll take you to the tower,
but I'm not leaving the island.

03:53.440 --> 03:56.235
- What?
- There's no place for me back there.

03:56.318 --> 03:58.560
This is my home now.

04:19.383 --> 04:21.218
Hello, Jack.

04:23.345 --> 04:24.930
We need to talk.

04:56.170 --> 04:58.411
- What did Ben say?
- Can we kill him?

04:58.505 --> 05:00.716
Is it possible
to turn this equipment off?

05:01.842 --> 05:02.874
What?

05:02.968 --> 05:05.262
The jamming equipment,
can you turn it off?

05:05.345 --> 05:09.130
- Sure. Ben gave us the code.
- You are the only ones who have it?

05:09.224 --> 05:10.976
Yeah. Why?

05:11.059 --> 05:14.646
What would happen
if the station were to be flooded?

05:14.730 --> 05:17.107
The casing for the equipment
is waterproof.

05:17.191 --> 05:18.650
It'll keep going forever.

05:18.734 --> 05:21.570
- Then why do you need to be here?
- Because Ben told us to.

05:21.653 --> 05:24.145
- We were following orders.
- You never asked why?

05:24.239 --> 05:28.285
No. Because I trust him.
And I trust Jacob.

05:28.368 --> 05:30.443
The minute I start questioning orders,

05:30.537 --> 05:34.958
this whole thing, everything that
we're doing here falls apart.

05:37.169 --> 05:39.004
She makes an excellent point.

06:00.150 --> 06:03.278
No. Please.

06:03.362 --> 06:06.365
I'm sorry, Bonnie.
I, too, am following orders.

06:08.617 --> 06:09.733
Hey!

06:17.918 --> 06:22.381
No, Des. Des! Don't! We need her.

06:46.905 --> 06:49.366
I'm Benjamin.
We haven't had the pleasure.

06:49.450 --> 06:51.285
Don't talk to him.

06:53.662 --> 06:56.290
- What do you want?
- Just a moment of your time.

06:57.583 --> 07:01.879
- To talk. You and me. Alone.
- For what?

07:01.962 --> 07:04.423
Jack, you've just killed
seven of my people.

07:04.506 --> 07:06.998
The least you can give me
is five minutes.

07:11.472 --> 07:12.587
He alone?

07:12.681 --> 07:15.173
There's only two sets of tracks.
His and hers.

07:23.776 --> 07:25.652
Five minutes.

07:44.171 --> 07:47.508
I'm sorry, there are no more
refills left on this prescription.

07:51.720 --> 07:55.724
Well, that's a mistake.
I only refilled it twice.

07:55.808 --> 07:59.259
- Could you check again?
- I did check it again, Dr Shephard.

07:59.353 --> 08:02.439
And that was the third refill,
so there's nothing I can do.

08:04.024 --> 08:06.318
I've got another prescription
right here.

08:06.401 --> 08:10.572
Hey. I know you. You're the hero.

08:10.656 --> 08:13.450
- I'm not a hero.
- Yeah. We saw it on TV.

08:13.534 --> 08:16.453
Hey, lady, just give this guy
whatever he needs.

08:16.537 --> 08:20.405
- Do you know what he did?
- Here it is. Here. Oxycodone.

08:20.499 --> 08:22.960
You can't write a prescription
for yourself.

08:23.043 --> 08:25.118
That's Dr Christian Shephard.

08:25.212 --> 08:27.287
I'm Dr Jack Shephard.
He's my father.

08:27.381 --> 08:30.050
- I'll call his office.
- He's out of town right now.

08:30.134 --> 08:32.428
Well, I'm sure somebody in the office...

08:33.429 --> 08:35.556
Don't bother.

08:50.487 --> 08:52.030
Have a seat.

08:59.955 --> 09:03.323
Not so long ago, Jack,
I made a decision

09:03.417 --> 09:07.463
that took the lives
of over 40 people in a single day.

09:10.466 --> 09:15.210
I'm telling you this because
history is about to repeat itself.

09:15.304 --> 09:17.796
- Right here. Right now.
- Let me guess.

09:18.515 --> 09:21.393
You've got us surrounded
and if I don't do what you say,

09:21.477 --> 09:25.981
- you're gonna kill all my people.
- No, Jack, you are.

09:29.902 --> 09:33.322
- How am I gonna do that, Ben?
- The woman you're travelling with.

09:33.405 --> 09:36.492
The one who parachuted onto the island
from a helicopter.

09:37.451 --> 09:39.693
She's not who she says she is.

09:41.288 --> 09:43.613
- She's not?
- No. She's not.

09:45.000 --> 09:46.032
Then who is she?

09:46.126 --> 09:48.201
She's a representative of some people

09:48.295 --> 09:51.340
who have been trying
to find this island, Jack.

09:52.424 --> 09:55.177
She's one of the bad guys.

09:55.260 --> 09:57.752
Oh, I almost forgot.

09:57.846 --> 10:00.849
You're the... you're the good guys.

10:00.933 --> 10:04.269
Jack, listen to me.
If you phone her boat,

10:04.353 --> 10:08.816
every single living person
on this island will be killed.

10:13.153 --> 10:16.573
So here's what has to happen.
Get that device.

10:17.658 --> 10:21.359
The phone she carries with her
and give it to me.

10:21.453 --> 10:24.873
I will turn around
and will go back to my people.

10:24.957 --> 10:27.584
You will turn around
and go back to your people.

10:27.668 --> 10:30.129
I'm not going anywhere.

10:39.555 --> 10:42.224
- May I have my walkie back?
- What?

10:42.307 --> 10:45.310
There's something you need to hear.
Please.

10:55.154 --> 10:56.488
Thank you.

10:59.783 --> 11:01.493
Tom? Are you there?

11:03.245 --> 11:05.456
<i>Yeah. I'm here.</i>

11:06.123 --> 11:08.083
Your plan killed seven of my people,

11:08.167 --> 11:11.503
but the ones that you failed to kill
are now holding your friends,

11:11.587 --> 11:14.298
Jin, Sayid, Bernard, at gunpoint.

11:14.381 --> 11:16.759
<i>Jack</i>, <i>don't give him any...</i>

11:16.842 --> 11:19.470
- <i>Stop! Leave him alone!</i>
- <i>I said shut up!</i>

11:21.096 --> 11:24.308
And what's to stop me
from snapping your neck?

11:24.391 --> 11:28.093
Tom, unless you hear my voice
in one minute, shoot all three of them.

11:28.187 --> 11:29.302
<i>Got it.</i>

11:29.938 --> 11:31.982
<i>I said don't move.</i>

11:35.694 --> 11:39.448
- Bring me the phone, Jack.
- <i>Don't negotiate with him.</i>

11:40.074 --> 11:43.358
- <i>Gag them.</i>
- <i>No.</i>

11:43.452 --> 11:45.287
- Forty seconds.
- No.

11:45.370 --> 11:47.998
I'm getting them all off the island.
All of them.

11:48.082 --> 11:50.793
Let me ask you,
why do you want to leave the island?

11:50.876 --> 11:54.244
What is it that you so desperately
want to get back to?

11:54.755 --> 11:56.913
You have no one.
Your father's dead.

11:57.007 --> 11:59.583
Your wife left you,
moved on with another man.

12:00.177 --> 12:04.838
Can you just not wait to get back to
the hospital? Get back to fixing things?

12:04.932 --> 12:09.561
It's 20 seconds now.
Just get me the phone, Jack.

12:09.645 --> 12:12.564
- No.
- Ten seconds. Bring me the phone.

12:12.648 --> 12:14.806
- I'm not bluffing.
- I won't do it!

12:14.900 --> 12:16.860
- Five. Four. Three.
- No.

12:19.071 --> 12:20.572
No!

12:28.455 --> 12:30.447
I'm so sorry, Jack.

13:01.613 --> 13:03.115
Tom, you there?

13:05.159 --> 13:07.619
Yeah, Jack. I hear you.

13:07.703 --> 13:11.238
I'm going to lead my people
up to the radio tower

13:12.082 --> 13:15.919
and I'm going to make a call.
And I'm going to get them all rescued.

13:16.003 --> 13:17.504
Every one of them.

13:18.672 --> 13:23.333
And then I'm gonna come find you.
And I'm gonna kill you.

13:35.314 --> 13:37.065
- What's the code?
- Go away.

13:37.149 --> 13:39.474
Let's get this over with.
What's the code?

13:39.568 --> 13:41.893
- She's not gonna tell you.
- Yeah, she will.

13:41.987 --> 13:43.103
Why do you say that?

13:43.197 --> 13:45.272
It's my destiny to turn off that jammer.

13:45.365 --> 13:48.368
OK, Bonnie. We're both
gonna die down here, all right?

13:48.452 --> 13:50.162
Let's be perfectly honest,

13:50.245 --> 13:53.457
one-eyed maniac killed your friend
and shot you in the back.

13:53.540 --> 13:57.377
It would appear that your
glorious leader, Ben, put him up to it.

13:57.878 --> 14:00.370
Are you a sodding idiot?

14:01.215 --> 14:05.511
You have the opportunity
to make Ben very, very angry.

14:05.594 --> 14:08.003
Why would you not take that?

14:13.644 --> 14:15.886
- Five, four, five.
- What?

14:15.979 --> 14:18.555
- Eight, seven, seven...
- Is that a code?

14:18.649 --> 14:21.819
- five, five, four, three, seven, six...
- Wait. Start again.

14:21.902 --> 14:24.738
Start from the beginning.
Bonnie, from the beginning.

14:24.822 --> 14:27.991
Bonnie, start again. Bonnie.
Bonnie. Wake up. Wake up.

14:28.075 --> 14:30.869
- Start again. Start again.
- <i>Good Vibrations.</i>

14:31.620 --> 14:33.163
What?

14:33.247 --> 14:36.667
Beach Boys. <i>Good Vibrations.</i>

14:39.420 --> 14:44.498
On the keypad. Numbers, they're notes.

14:48.762 --> 14:51.140
It was programmed by a musician.

15:16.707 --> 15:19.918
Tie him up. He's coming with us.

15:40.314 --> 15:41.857
What?

15:45.652 --> 15:47.237
Alex...

15:49.907 --> 15:51.283
...this is your mother.

16:21.271 --> 16:23.107
Will you help me tie him up?

16:42.668 --> 16:44.336
What happened? What'd he say?

16:45.045 --> 16:47.965
It's not important.
Just get everyone together.

16:48.048 --> 16:50.290
Jack, your knuckles.

17:02.980 --> 17:04.888
What happened?

17:07.359 --> 17:08.902
He killed them.

17:11.738 --> 17:15.409
Bernard, Jin, Sayid.
All three of them.

17:18.078 --> 17:22.082
He radioed the beach.
And I let it happen.

17:27.087 --> 17:30.340
I had to let it happen.

17:31.008 --> 17:34.011
We can't tell Rose or Sun. Not yet.

17:34.094 --> 17:35.721
We've got to keep moving.

17:35.804 --> 17:39.308
I promised Sayid that
we would keep moving.

17:41.018 --> 17:42.561
So why did you bring him back?

17:45.189 --> 17:46.982
Why didn't you just kill him?

17:47.065 --> 17:49.526
Because I want him to see it,

17:51.403 --> 17:54.323
to experience the moment
that we get off this island.

17:54.406 --> 17:58.911
And I want him to know that he failed.

18:04.708 --> 18:06.376
And then I'll kill him.

18:10.047 --> 18:12.841
It was an order, Tom.
We had to follow it.

18:12.925 --> 18:16.459
Ben doesn't know what the hell
he's talking about. He's lost it!

18:16.553 --> 18:18.597
I mean, look at what they did to us!

18:18.680 --> 18:23.102
Instead of putting three bullets in the
sand, we should've killed them for real!

18:34.363 --> 18:36.855
All they got left
is three guys and four guns.

18:36.949 --> 18:39.660
And all we've got, James,
are two people and no guns.

18:41.453 --> 18:42.621
We'll wait till night.

18:42.704 --> 18:45.030
Night won't change
the fact we're unarmed.

18:45.124 --> 18:48.658
If you want to kill yourself, fine,
but before you go and...

18:51.588 --> 18:52.840
You hear that?

19:11.316 --> 19:12.484
Ryan!

19:20.617 --> 19:22.035
Stay in the bus, Hugo.

19:52.566 --> 19:54.401
Stay right there, Tom.

20:01.325 --> 20:04.745
OK. I give up.

20:14.797 --> 20:16.955
That's for taking the kid off the raft.

20:22.846 --> 20:24.723
Dude, it was over. He surrendered.

20:27.434 --> 20:29.103
I didn't believe him.

21:10.811 --> 21:13.105
What are you doing, Dr Shephard?

21:13.188 --> 21:14.898
I was just...

21:14.982 --> 21:17.276
I was just checking the...

21:17.901 --> 21:19.570
The Arlen charts.

21:19.653 --> 21:22.114
I wanted to see how the operation went.

21:22.197 --> 21:25.868
I left three messages
on your voicemail. You didn't get them?

21:26.493 --> 21:28.245
My phone's broken.

21:31.540 --> 21:33.125
Let's go to my office, Jack.

21:33.917 --> 21:35.377
For what?

21:35.461 --> 21:37.953
We need to have a talk. Come on.

21:39.882 --> 21:43.500
I know that you're new around here,
so you don't know much about me.

21:43.594 --> 21:46.513
I know enough.
So let's just walk down to my office...

21:46.597 --> 21:50.434
If you've got something to say to me,
you can say it to me right here.

21:53.061 --> 21:55.303
Will you excuse us, please?

22:00.402 --> 22:04.271
Mrs Arlen, the woman you saved,
woke up in recovery about two hours ago.

22:04.364 --> 22:06.033
She was in some pain,

22:06.116 --> 22:09.870
but highly responsive
to the reflex tests and entirely lucid.

22:10.662 --> 22:14.114
Well, that's... That's great.

22:14.208 --> 22:18.587
But then she described the series
of events that caused her accident.

22:20.255 --> 22:22.382
She says she was driving over the bridge

22:22.466 --> 22:26.970
when she saw a man standing on top
of the railing, about to jump off.

22:29.264 --> 22:32.549
She was distracted
and lost control of her car.

22:32.643 --> 22:37.147
She ran into the median, rolled over
and was hit by the van behind her.

22:40.400 --> 22:42.861
So the obvious question here, Jack,

22:43.403 --> 22:45.948
is how did you
get to that flaming car so fast?

22:46.031 --> 22:49.399
What were you doing on that bridge?

22:57.292 --> 23:00.295
Do you know how many years
I've worked at this hospital?

23:01.130 --> 23:04.748
Do you know anything about me?

23:06.260 --> 23:10.681
Do you have any idea
what I've been through?

23:11.140 --> 23:13.934
How much have you had
to drink today, Jack?

23:14.852 --> 23:17.177
OK, I'll tell you what. You do this.

23:17.271 --> 23:21.056
You get my father down here.
Get him down here right now.

23:21.150 --> 23:24.111
And if I'm drunker than he is,
you can fire me.

23:26.572 --> 23:30.909
Don't you look at me like that.
Don't you pity me.

23:30.993 --> 23:33.485
- I'm trying to help you.
- You can't help me!

24:05.319 --> 24:08.155
<i>Attention</i>, <i>Others! Come in</i>, <i>Others!</i>

24:08.947 --> 24:12.732
<i>If you're listening to this</i>, <i>I want</i>
<i>you to know that we got you bastards.</i>

24:12.826 --> 24:15.746
<i>And unless the rest of you</i>
<i>want to be blown up</i>,

24:15.829 --> 24:18.624
<i>you best stay away from our beach.</i>

24:18.707 --> 24:21.543
- Hurley?
- Jack?

24:22.377 --> 24:25.714
- <i>Where are you? What's going on?</i>
- Dude. I'm back at the beach.

24:25.798 --> 24:27.257
What?

24:27.341 --> 24:29.635
Yeah, I went back
to help Juliet and Sawyer.

24:29.718 --> 24:31.178
I saved them.

24:31.804 --> 24:34.723
- They're OK? Juliet...
- Everyone's fine.

24:34.807 --> 24:39.968
Me, Sawyer, Juliet, Sayid, Jin, Bernard.

24:40.062 --> 24:41.772
- We're all...
- Wait.

24:43.857 --> 24:47.069
Bernard and Jin and Sayid,
they're with you?

24:47.152 --> 24:49.644
Yeah, dude. I told you.
I saved them all.

25:03.168 --> 25:05.712
Stay where you are,
we're almost up to the tower.

25:05.796 --> 25:07.673
- <i>You'll be safer there.</i>
- I got you.

25:07.756 --> 25:10.551
We'll stay put until you, like,
you know, phone home.

25:13.470 --> 25:16.140
What about Charlie?
Did he make it back yet?

25:16.223 --> 25:19.810
Not yet, but they're probably
paddling home as we speak.

25:19.893 --> 25:21.728
Don't worry, I'm sure he's fine.

25:33.532 --> 25:36.535
Des, there's diving gear
on those racks, yeah?

25:37.411 --> 25:39.569
- Aye. There's plenty.
- Take care of that.

25:39.663 --> 25:43.114
- I'll tap out <i>Good Vibrations.</i>
- All right, mate.

25:43.208 --> 25:44.877
- Hey, Desmond?
- Aye.

25:44.960 --> 25:46.670
You get any flashes?

25:48.589 --> 25:50.048
No. Nothing.

25:52.342 --> 25:54.835
- Meet you back here then.
- Aye.

26:47.564 --> 26:49.233
So much for fate.

27:00.494 --> 27:02.246
Incoming transmission.

27:06.500 --> 27:08.794
<i>Hello? Can you hear me?</i>

27:09.545 --> 27:13.382
- Yes. Yes, I can hear you.
- <i>Who is this? Who am I speaking to?</i>

27:13.465 --> 27:15.509
Charlie. Charlie Pace.

27:15.592 --> 27:20.139
I'm a survivor of flight 815.
Oceanic flight 815.

27:20.222 --> 27:21.974
<i>Where are you?</i>

27:22.057 --> 27:23.892
We're on an island. We're alive.

27:23.976 --> 27:26.103
<i>An island? Where?</i>
<i>What's your location?</i>

27:26.186 --> 27:31.400
- I don't know. Who's this?
- <i>This is Penelope. Penelope Widmore.</i>

27:31.483 --> 27:33.944
- <i>How did you get this frequency?</i>
- Desmond!

27:35.779 --> 27:37.614
Desmond!

27:38.824 --> 27:42.661
- <i>Did you just say "Desmond"?</i>
- Yeah! He's here. He's with me.

27:42.745 --> 27:44.955
- <i>Is he OK?</i>
- He's brilliant.

27:45.038 --> 27:47.583
- Hey, are you on the boat?
- <i>What boat?</i>

27:47.666 --> 27:52.494
Your boat. Eighty miles off shore.
Naomi parachuted.

27:52.588 --> 27:55.591
<i>I'm not on a boat. Who's Naomi?</i>

28:11.482 --> 28:15.100
<i>Hello? Is Desmond there?</i>

28:15.194 --> 28:18.645
<i>Desmond</i>, <i>can you hear me? Desmond!</i>

28:28.040 --> 28:30.834
- <i>Can you hear me?</i>
- Penny!

28:30.918 --> 28:32.117
No!

28:53.607 --> 28:54.806
Charlie!

30:38.545 --> 30:41.121
- Really, it's OK, sweetie.
- What's the matter?

30:42.049 --> 30:44.802
I don't know.
I think he's just a bit scared.

30:44.885 --> 30:46.470
Hard to blame him.

30:49.765 --> 30:52.340
- What is it?
- What's your boyfriend's name?

30:52.434 --> 30:55.062
- The rock star?
- Charlie. Why?

30:58.440 --> 31:00.025
Charlie just got us rescued.

31:05.280 --> 31:09.910
Jack! Jack, he did it!
Your friend bloody well did it!

31:09.993 --> 31:12.037
- What?
- The green light. It's on!

31:12.121 --> 31:14.248
- The jamming's stopped!
- Use it then.

31:14.331 --> 31:15.363
All right.

31:18.293 --> 31:20.869
<i>Four</i>, <i>four</i>, <i>two.</i>

31:24.299 --> 31:26.510
What's this?

31:26.593 --> 31:29.471
It's Rousseau's message,
still blocking the signal.

31:29.555 --> 31:31.682
It doesn't matter. We're here.

31:31.765 --> 31:34.893
<i>Iteration one</i>, <i>seven</i>, <i>five</i>, <i>five.</i>

32:09.928 --> 32:13.432
<i>Iteration one</i>, <i>seven</i>, <i>five</i>, <i>five</i>,

32:13.515 --> 32:15.976
<i>zero</i>, <i>four</i>, <i>four</i>, <i>five.</i>

32:27.863 --> 32:30.783
I recorded this 16 years ago.

32:30.866 --> 32:33.494
Three days before before you were born.

32:39.041 --> 32:40.876
I guess we don't need it anymore.

32:47.925 --> 32:49.124
All right. Do it.

32:56.225 --> 32:58.800
I can't get a signal in here.

33:15.744 --> 33:18.038
I'm getting something.

33:19.206 --> 33:22.876
It's gonna work. It's happening.
We're gonna get off of this island.

33:22.960 --> 33:25.035
I'll celebrate when we're home.

33:27.381 --> 33:31.677
Jack. I know you think
you're saving your people.

33:32.386 --> 33:35.921
But you need to stop this.
It's a mistake.

33:36.014 --> 33:39.768
- The mistake was listening to you.
- This will be your last chance, Jack.

33:39.852 --> 33:43.897
I'm telling you, making that call
is the beginning of the end.

33:43.981 --> 33:45.941
I've got it! I've got a signal!

33:47.526 --> 33:49.434
You don't know what you're doing.

33:49.528 --> 33:51.238
I know exactly what I'm doing.

34:08.130 --> 34:09.214
John!

34:09.298 --> 34:11.206
Step back, Jack.

34:20.350 --> 34:22.509
- What did you do?
- What I had to.

34:22.603 --> 34:23.885
Now step back.

34:31.069 --> 34:33.614
Stay away from the phone.

34:40.621 --> 34:43.874
- What are you doing, John?
- I don't want to shoot you.

34:43.957 --> 34:47.044
Do it, John. Shoot him.
Do it! You need...

34:53.717 --> 34:58.055
Please. Put the phone down.

34:59.515 --> 35:03.936
No. You're done
keeping me on this island.

35:09.608 --> 35:13.862
I will kill you if I have to.

35:13.946 --> 35:16.104
- Then do it, John.
- Jack.

35:32.464 --> 35:33.663
Jack.

35:36.301 --> 35:39.753
You're not supposed to do this.

35:43.934 --> 35:45.561
<i>Minkowski.</i>

35:47.980 --> 35:49.773
<i>Hello?</i>

35:53.277 --> 35:55.571
- Who is this?
- <i>Who is this?</i>

35:57.406 --> 36:00.117
My name's Jack Shephard. Are you...?

36:00.951 --> 36:04.455
- Are you on the boat? The freighter?
- <i>How'd you get this channel?</i>

36:04.997 --> 36:08.365
Naomi. Naomi told us about
your search team. About the boat.

36:09.001 --> 36:12.702
<i>Naomi? You found her?</i>
<i>Where is she? Who are you?</i>

36:14.089 --> 36:17.624
I'm one of the survivors
of Oceanic flight 815.

36:19.178 --> 36:22.796
- Can you get a fix on our location?
- <i>Hell yeah</i>, <i>we can.</i>

36:22.890 --> 36:25.851
<i>Sit tight. We'll be right there.</i>

37:05.182 --> 37:06.381
<i>Hello?</i>

37:08.227 --> 37:12.231
Hello? It's me.

37:14.191 --> 37:16.568
Wait. Don't hang up. Please.

37:19.363 --> 37:24.274
I know what you said.
I just... I just need to see you.

37:25.369 --> 37:26.620
Please.

37:28.330 --> 37:32.084
Yeah. Yeah, out at the airport.

37:33.836 --> 37:36.296
You know where.

37:38.173 --> 37:39.842
Thank you.

38:55.876 --> 38:57.503
- Hey.
- Hey.

39:01.882 --> 39:03.217
I saw you on the news.

39:05.052 --> 39:07.888
Still pulling people
out of burning wreckage?

39:07.971 --> 39:10.130
Old habits.

39:12.392 --> 39:14.103
You look terrible.

39:16.814 --> 39:18.273
Thanks.

39:20.818 --> 39:22.861
Why did you call me, Jack?

39:33.580 --> 39:35.624
I was hoping that you'd heard.

39:35.707 --> 39:37.835
That maybe you'd go to the funeral.

39:41.296 --> 39:42.923
Why would I go to the funeral?

39:55.811 --> 39:57.146
I've been flying a lot.

39:59.356 --> 40:01.681
- What?
- That golden pass that they gave us,

40:02.651 --> 40:04.278
I've been using it.

40:04.361 --> 40:09.439
Every Friday night I fly from LA

40:09.533 --> 40:15.122
to Tokyo or Singapore or Sydney.

40:18.083 --> 40:23.672
And then I get off and I have a drink
and then I fly home.

40:25.466 --> 40:26.633
Why?

40:30.053 --> 40:32.681
Because I want it to crash, Kate.

40:35.601 --> 40:38.854
I don't care
about anybody else onboard.

40:40.355 --> 40:43.807
Every little bump we hit or turbulence,

40:43.901 --> 40:47.352
I mean, I actually close my eyes

40:47.446 --> 40:52.326
and I pray that I can get back.

41:00.709 --> 41:05.047
- This is not gonna change.
- No, I'm sick of lying.

41:08.550 --> 41:10.177
We made a mistake.

41:16.642 --> 41:20.229
I have to go.
He's gonna be wondering where I am.

41:20.312 --> 41:21.344
Don't.

41:27.569 --> 41:32.366
- We were not supposed to leave.
- Yes, we were.

41:41.458 --> 41:42.918
Goodbye, Jack.

41:50.843 --> 41:53.303
We have to go back, Kate.

42:10.529 --> 42:12.823
We have to go back!
